}
}
#KEY "*thief*" "*steal*"  "*thiev*" {
#Attitude Wicked {
	"I refuse to answer to any base accusations!",
	"Thou cannot prove anything!"
		}
#Attitude Neutral {
	"A thief? I see thou hast been listening to malicious lies about us... 'gypsies,' to use thy own word.",
	"Freemen are not thieves! That is a malicious lie of the ignorant."
		}
#Attitude Goodhearted {
	"We have no need to steal, for nature meets all our needs.",
	"What could I possibly steal? I have everything I need!"
}
}
}
#Sophistication Low {
#Key "*job*", "*work*", "*what*do*do*", "*profession*", "*occupation*" {
#Attitude Wicked {
	"I got no leash 'round my neck.  I'm a freeman!",
	"Let others have their 'jobs.' I want the open road."
	}
#Attitude Neutral {
	"I'm a child o' the open road.  I wander 'round freely.",
	"I'm a wanderer, and take whatever comes to me."
	}
#Attitude Goodhearted {
	"I'm a freeman, and my job is to be who I am and ask nothin' more from anyone else.",
	"I'm happy wanderin' as my fortune may move me."
	}
	}
#KEY "*skill*" "*lock*" "*appraise*" "*hide*" "*camp*"  {
	#Attitude Wicked {
	"¡Aléjate! ¡No perderé el tiempo en ayudarte!",
"¡No te voy a enseñar nada! ¡No eres un hombre libre!",
"¡Tengo muchas habilidades! Cosas que te ayudarían, la verdad. Y no te las voy a enseñar."
			}
	#Attitude Neutral {
	"Podría mostrarte algunas cosas. Cosas útiles, apuesto. Sin embargo, tienes que gastar algo de dinero.",
"Podría enseñarte a observar mejor a la gente. O a asegurarme de que no te vean muy bien.",
"Por un precio podría enseñarte algunas cosas sobre acampar. Por un precio.",
"Puedo enseñarte a observar mejor las cosas. Cosas como la gente y lo que poseen."
			}
	#Attitude Goodhearted {
	"Podría enseñarte algunas cosas. Solo dame unas pocas monedas.",
"Tengo habilidades que podrían ayudarte. Podría enseñarte. Sin embargo, costará.",
"Si necesitas ayuda para acampar, podría ayudarte por un módico precio."
			}
		}
#KEY "*gypsy*" "*freeman*" "*gypsie*" {
#Attitude Wicked {
	"Thou got a problem with us?  Live and let live, I say.",
	"What's wrong with 'gypsies,' as thou calls us?  We're honest people who choose to live where we feel most comfortable at the moment."
	}
#Attitude Neutral {
	"I'm a true freeman, born and bred.",
	"Not everyone is lucky enough to be born a freeman. Thou might refer to us as gypsies, but we're a breed apart."
	}
#Attitude Goodhearted {
	"We freemen, or 'gypsies,' as thy people insist on calling us, are brothers to the road!",
	"Music, love and travel, that's the life of a freeman!"
}
}
#KEY "*thief*" "*steal*"  "*thiev*" {
#Attitude Wicked {
	"I refuse to answer to thee!",
	"Thou can't prove nothin'!"
		}
#Attitude Neutral {
	"A thief? I see thou've been listenin' to lies 'bout us... 'gypsies,' to use thy own word.",
	"Freemen aren't thieves! That's a malicious lie of the stupid."
		}
#Attitude Goodhearted {
	"We got no need to steal, 'cause nature meets all our needs.",
	"What could I steal? I got everything I need!"
}
}
}
}
